      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the technicality of ratification, but that feels like a distinction without a difference. If the 'managed participation' you mentioned forces countries to follow rules they didn't actually want just to stay part of the system, hasn't the essence of sovereignty already been lost? It feels less like 'participation' and more like a slow-motion takeover by bureaucrats who aren't accountable to any actual voters.",
