      "content": "Your frustration addresses the fundamental tension between asserting absolute power and voluntarily accepting binding international constraints, which redefines the modern concept of sovereignty from exclusive control to shared responsibility. The perception of a bureaucratic takeover often stems from the reality that states cannot operate effectively in an interconnected world without adhering to these rules, even when those rules limit immediate domestic choices. Ultimately, while the losses of traditional sovereignty are real and significant, the shift represents a pragmatic trade-off where states exchange absolute autonomy for a framework capable of addressing complex global challenges that lone governments cannot solve alone.",
